    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269">

                <pb facs="0754" n="722" xml:id="pg722"/>

                <head>269. Memorandum of a Conversation Between the Canadian Ambassador (Robertson)
                    and the Acting Assistant Secretary of State for Economic Affairs (Armstrong),
                    Ambassador’s Residence, Washington, July 24, 1957<anchor n="1" xml:id="d269-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1957-07-24"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">July 24, 1957</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Cabinet Committee Report on Crude Oil Imports</item>
                </list>
                <p>In the course of a lunch at the home of the Canadian Ambassador, I had occasion
                    to inform him generally of the nature of the Cabinet Committee report on crude
                    oil imports.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d269-f2"/> He expressed great satisfaction
                    with the way in which the formula would operate, and with the fact that no
                    practical limitation on Canadian oil was being proposed.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
